q706f (Lenovo Tab P12 Pro, SM8250) kernel series on top of upstream Linux v7.3.4
================================================================================

Base: Linux v7.3.4 (stable, tag object 8310b43a724c, commit 7595a62d45ee, 2026-11-10).
Tarball: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v7.x/linux-7.3.4.tar.xz
sha256:  b11b6df8295e8e991ff040b71aaa4994a8b55caa23b6b092907f195b5840fd1f
         (as listed in kernel.org's v7.x/sha256sums.asc; the PGP signature of that
         list was not verified here)

The patches apply in file-name order with `patch -p1 -F0` (no fuzz, no offsets needed)
on a pristine extraction of the tarball. The result is byte-for-byte identical to
sources/linux-desktop (verified with `diff -r` on a fresh extraction).

Patches
-------
0001-upstream-PCI-qcom-honor-iommu-cells.patch
    Upstream commit 5121d76cb9dd (v7.4-rc1). The only part of silime's 7.3.0-dev delta
    that this tablet needs: since v7.3-rc the sm8250.dtsi PCIe iommu-map entries carry
    two IOMMU cells, and without this fix the BDF-to-SID table for bus 1 (the QCA6390
    Wi-Fi) is programmed from misparsed cells. silime carried an earlier revision of the
    same patch; the upstream version is used.

0002-q706f-port-on-v7.3.4.patch
    The q706f support ( taken from silime
    7.1.0-dev: board DTS, panel, charger/fuel gauge, CS35L45/AS33970/ES7210 audio,
    q6afe/sm8250 machine driver changes, haptics, cameras, pogo keyboard/touchpad HID
    quirks, nb7vpq904m, fastrpc, ...) re-applied on v7.3.4. Differences from the 7.3-rc3
    version of the patch:
      - drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c: MT_QUIRK_NO_MODE_REPORTS is BIT(27) (BIT(26) is
        MT_QUIRK_IGNORE_FEATURE_ID_MISMATCH upstream now); mt_get_feature() already has
        the `td` local upstream.
      - drivers/input/misc/Kconfig: INPUT_QCOM_SPMI_HAPTICS placed after
        INPUT_PMIC8XXX_PWRKEY (its old neighbour, silime's INPUT_QCOM_HV_HAPTICS, is not
        carried).
      - dongwoon,dw9768 binding: only the dw9763 compatible is added (silime's dw9800k
        entry is not carried).
      - drivers/misc/fastrpc.c: sits on top of the reworked upstream Audio PD
        remote-heap code (v7.3 final); no functional change to the patch.

0101 ... 0111  (the project patches; numbered as in the older, unpublished 7.1 series + 100)
    0101 goodix-berlin stylus support            0107 battery charge limits (DTS + charger)
    0102 DTS: stylus + speakers-only sound       0109 goodix-berlin stylus tip/hover/tilt
    0104 DTS: CTN730 pen charger                 0110 pm8150b charger ICL + thermal
    0105 pogo keyboard SW_TABLET_MODE            0111 as33970: no firmware download at probe
    0106 panel amsa26zp01 60 Hz
    The *.needs-approval patches of the project are not part of the series.

0014, 0015  (DTS, integrated 16.11.2026; previously *.needs-approval, proven in B2/B3af)
    0014 disables the unused QCE (crypto engine) node, 0015 the unused PCIe2 controller.

0113, 0114  (integrated 16.11.2026; proven in B3af on both slots since 14.11.2026)
    0113 goodix-berlin: send the pen on/off command (0x14/0x15 at 0x10174), sysfs pen_mode;
         without it the GT9916 never reports the pen after a power cycle.
    0114 DTS: rear camera DW9768 lens actuator at 0x0c on CCI0 (manual focus).

0201-backport-ufs-qcom-enable-only-lane-clocks.patch
    Upstream commit f07317a8d57f (v7.4-rc1). Replaces the project's pending
    0013-ufs-qcom-lane-clks-enable-balance.patch.needs-approval (same bug; the upstream
    fix also contains the "already enabled" check that 0013 adds).

0202-backport-sm8250-gcc-cx-power-domain.patch
    Upstream commit 389a0144c511 (v7.4-rc1), DT only: GCC GDSCs become subdomains of
    RPMh CX. Works with the v7.3.4 gdsc code (gdsc_register() parents the GDSCs to the
    provider's power domain); the 7.4 driver clean-up 361b375a4bb1 is not required.
    Drop this patch first if a GDSC consumer misbehaves.

0203a ... 0203e  (integrated 16.11.2026; proven in B2/B3af)
    Adreno GMU / drm-msm series (Akhil P Oommen): CX power-domain link, standalone GPU
    component, GMU driver attach; fixes the GPU suspend/resume path.

0204-clk-qcom-camcc-sm8250-xo-active-only.patch   camcc parent = XO active-only
0205-pci-qcom-no-hotplug-on-q706f-root-port.patch  PCIe root port without hot-plug, so
    the Wi-Fi link goes to L2 and the host is deinitialised in s2idle
0206-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8250-cpu-icc-active-only.patch  CPU-DDR ICC paths ACTIVE_ONLY
    (also carried by other SM8250 projects as "1118")
    (0204-0206 integrated 16.11.2026; proven in B3af)

0118-asoc-qcom-sm8250-release-afe-port-clocks-on-shutdown.patch  backend shutdown sends a
    0 Hz request (enable = 0) for the MI2S/TDM bit clock enabled in startup(); without it
    the LPASS clock stays voted in the ADSP and the SoC never reaches CXSD (integrated
    16.11.2026; RAM-boot test r13: first CXSD with the full system)

Without 0118, with 0014, 0015, 0113, 0114 and 0203a-0206 the series reproduces, source for source, the
B3af kernel that runs on boot_a/boot_b since 14.11.2026 (verified 16.11.2026 with
diff -r against the B3af source tree).

Still pending (not applied by the build): 0112 (soundwire, not needed), 0115 (panel
probe-time supply vote, untested), 0116 (USB-PD 9 V sink PDO + 4 A charging, 9 V not
tested yet), 0117 (pm8150b Quick Charge 9 V request, QC path not exercised yet).

Evaluated and not applied
-------------------------
ath11k "fix unbalanced IRQ enable/disable during suspend/resume"
    Upstream commit e56c9d429ba0. It fixes a regression introduced by f7a74e131d3f
    ("wifi: ath11k: disable interrupts during firmware crash recovery"), which is in
    v7.4-rc only and is not in v7.3.4; the patch does not apply and there is nothing to
    fix on 7.3.4.

Dropped from silime 7.3.0-dev
-----------------------------
silime's 7.3.0-dev is SM8550 (Meizu 20 Infinity) work on top of a post-rc3 mainline
snapshot; it has no q706f support. Everything except the PCIe fix above is dropped, see
docs/KERNEL-7.3.4-STARE.md for the list and the reasons.

Recreating the tree and building
--------------------------------
    scripts/desktop/build-kernel.sh     # tarball (sha256 checked) + this series -> sources/linux-desktop,
                                        # config, Image.gz, dtbs, modules -> out/desktop/kernel/
    scripts/desktop/kernel-cycle.sh build   # the above + ctn730 module + out/desktop/ubuntu-boot.img

By hand:
    tar -xf linux-7.3.4.tar.xz && cd linux-7.3.4
    for p in /path/to/scripts/desktop/patches/[0-9]*.patch; do patch -p1 -F0 < "$p"; done

Do not use `git apply` from inside a subdirectory of another git work tree: it silently
skips files outside that subdirectory.

Config: scripts/desktop/config-pmos-q706f-6.11 -> olddefconfig -> merge_config with
q706f-desktop.config, q706f-7.3-renames.config, q706f-7.3.4-extra.config -> olddefconfig.
Kernel release string: 7.3.4 (LOCALVERSION is forced empty).

Not applied
-----------
*.needs-approval files in this directory are proposals waiting for the owner's decision
(they still apply cleanly on this tree). The former 7.1 series is kept for reference in
../patches-7.1/ (0013 there is superseded by 0201 here).

0121-wifi-ath11k-pci-unbind-across-system-suspend.patch  (integrated 20.11.2026)
    Module parameter ath11k_pci.unbind_in_suspend (default off; on in
    /etc/modprobe.d/q706f-ath11k.conf): the PCI device is unbound at PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE and
    bound again after resume. With the driver bound, only the first s2idle after boot
    reaches CX collapse; with it, CXSD on every suspend (overnight ~52 mA vs ~97 mA).

0123-asoc-cs35l45-tempmon-override-and-irq-names.patch  (integrated 20.11.2026)
    TEMPMON global override around the speaker-protection firmware (as the vendor driver
    does) and correct names for the amplifier error interrupts. The protection firmware
    itself still does not process audio on mainline; speakers stay on the bypass route
    with the UCM volume cap.

Other files:
    0119 *.rejected   AS33970 supplies not always-on (rejected: the sound card no longer probes)
    0120 *.pending    q6dsp-lpass-clocks: drvdata before clock registration (ADSP restart crash)
    0121b *.pending   debug-only ath11k experiment (firmware boot in resume instead of resume_early)
    0122 *.pending    s5k5e9: propagate I2C errors, start at 1x gain (optional)
    0124 *.pending    cs35l45: minimum time in hibernation before wake (no effect alone)
    0899 *.debug      debug-only (PCIe controller kept off)
